-- #1617/#1618 ACCEPTANCE PIN — the half of the bystander property that no
-- BUILD-executing corpus can carry.
--
-- The arrow/effect impl-head tags are a ROUTING fix, but the projection they
-- moved is also read by things that decide ACCEPTANCE. This file poses BOTH of
-- those readers and asserts the ONE thing that must not change: `medaka check`
-- reports NOTHING. The golden is an empty diagnostics array, which is why this
-- fixture cannot pass vacuously — a narrowing emits `T-AMBIGUOUS-INSTANCE` and
-- the byte-compare fails.
--
--   * `szc []` fixes nothing, so the `Sz` constraint is UNDETERMINED.
--     `checkUndeterminedObligation`'s RULE 3 rejects when the interface has
--     `implCountForIfaceU >= 2`, counted over the `ImplUniverse` iface->head-tag
--     SET. `Bool` is the only head that set may contain: an arrow head and an
--     effect-carrying head are not head type constructors, exactly as the
--     headless impls they used to be filed beside. Count 1, no error.
--   * `conv 1` needs `groundOneObligation` to find the UNIQUE `Conv` impl at
--     head tag `Int`. The effect-headed sibling must not be a second match, or
--     `b` stays undetermined and a `Display` cascade rejects at `println`.
--
-- Neither the arrow impl nor either effect impl is ever dispatched to. That is
-- the point: this is "unrelated code still behaves", posed at the two readers
-- the change perturbs.
--
-- MEASURED on three cold-built arms — base `aaa43716` check 0, branch
-- `a8a226cb` check 1 (`Ambiguous instance for Sz`), amended branch check 0.
--
-- ⚠️ CHECK-ONLY ON PURPOSE. `medaka build` REJECTS this file on every arm
-- including base: an undetermined constraint leaves the site's route unstamped
-- and the emitter E-PANICs `no impl of method 'szc' for type 'List'`. That is a
-- separate, pre-existing defect — a single-impl `Sz` with no arrow and no
-- effect anywhere in the program reproduces it on base `aaa43716` — and it is
-- why the sibling fixture `test/engine_fixtures/fun_head_impl_bystander.mdk`,
-- which must build, carries only the `Conv` half.
interface Sz a where
  sz : a -> Int
  szc : List a -> Int

impl Sz Bool where
  sz _ = 7
  szc _ = 21

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Sz (Int -> Int) where
  sz _ = 5
  szc _ = 55

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Sz (<Stdout> Float) where
  sz _ = 6
  szc _ = 66

interface Conv a b where
  conv : a -> b

impl Conv Int Bool where
  conv n = n > 0

-- present, never dispatched to
impl Conv (<Stdout> Int) String where
  conv _ = "never"

main = println (sz True, szc [], conv 1)
